Explanation  
We iteratively  
1) inspect Citi Bike data,  
2) find 2016 trips,  
3) locate the 20 most-frequent routes,  
4) grab rounded co-ordinates for joining,  
5) compute average bike duration for each of those routes,  
6) compute average yellow-taxi duration between the same rounded co-ordinate pairs,  
7) compare the two to see where bikes are faster,  
8–10) pick the route that is faster than taxis yet has the longest average bike time, and finally output just its start-station name, which satisfies the question.
